    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "On the official distance-three support packet, label each exceptional root by (Y_a,[C(a)]_r), where Y_a is its matching-free boundary e-th-power value and [.]_r is the class modulo r-th powers. With mu=[-product_(t in T)C(t)]_r, a perfect matching satisfies both every boundary gate and every dual row-product gate exactly when the label multiset is invariant under (y,g)|->(-y,mu/g). This reconstructs all joint-admissible matchings and forces the aggregate obstruction Res(A,C)/(-Res(B,C))^e in (F_q^*)^r.",
